APPLICATION AND DATA

  VA FileMan 22.2 — MIXED PROVENANCE, measured 2026-07-26 by reading all 861
      routines of the pinned source (do not restate this from memory; re-measure
      when the pin moves):

        774 of 861 routines carry, in the routine source itself:
            ";;Based on Medsphere Systems Corporation's MSC FileMan 1051."
            ";;Licensed under the terms of the Apache License, Version 2.0."
          — Apache-2.0, Medsphere Systems Corporation lineage, submitted to
            OSEHRA by the VISTA Expertise Network.

         87 of 861 routines carry no such notice (the DDE*/DI* set) — United
            States Government work, no licence terms asserted.

        797 of 861 additionally carry ";;Per VA Directive 6402, this routine
            should not be modified." That is a VA internal directive about
            running FileMan unmodified, not a licence term binding a third
            party; it is recorded because the image honours it in substance
            (see the change statement below).

      Obtained from the WorldVistA/VistA-VEHU-M mirror at a pinned commit, with
      every routine byte verified against a committed checksum manifest before
      the build.

      APACHE-2.0 COMPLIANCE, as satisfied by this image:
        §4(a) a copy of the License travels with the artifact — /opt/licenses/
              Apache-2.0.txt (also this NOTICE at /opt/licenses/NOTICE).
        §4(b) attribution notices are RETAINED: the routines ship as source in
              /opt/lib/r with their notice lines intact.
        §4(b) STATEMENT OF CHANGES. The FileMan routines are installed VERBATIM
              and are not edited. Two mechanical changes are made and are
              disclosed here:
                (1) five routines are COPIED to `%`-names required by a
                    Kernel-free GT.M/YottaDB engine (DIDT→%DT, DIDTC→%DTC,
                    DIRCR→%RCR, DIIS→%ZIS, DIISS→%ZISS). Only the routine label
                    line differs; the body, including the Apache notice, is
                    copied unchanged.
                (2) two routines that are NOT FileMan and NOT derived from it
                    are added by vista-forge: FMPOCREN (performs the copy above)
                    and ZOSVSTUB (a minimal %ZOSV, which standalone FileMan does
                    not ship for GT.M). Both are vista-forge code under this
                    repo's terms.
              `^DINIT` is DRIVEN through its normal interactive dialog, not
              patched.

