Combined-work status — RULED 2026-07-26
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

CORRESPONDING SOURCE (AGPL). The complete source this image was built from —
all ten contributing repositories at their exact build commits — is published
in this image's own public repository:

  https://github.com/vista-forge/m-devbox/tree/main/releases

  m-devbox-<version>-corresponding-source.tar.gz  (+ .sha256)

That bundle is the discharge of the AGPL corresponding-source obligation
carried by YottaDB and by vista-forge's own AGPL code. It is verifiable, not
merely offered: each repository is archived at the commit the image was staged
from, the binaries are built against committed pins rather than working trees,
and the image's own acceptance gates refuse a mismatch (G25 licences, G27 pins).

RULING. Ship as AGPL-3.0-or-later. Apache-2.0 (VA FileMan, the extensions,
code-server) and GPL-2.0 (git) are all one-way compatible INTO an AGPL
aggregate, which is the direction this image goes, so the licences do not
conflict. Full analysis: docs/licensing/m-devbox-combined-work-disposition.md
in the vista-forge `docs` repo. Nothing here is a legal conclusion.

FILEMAN IS NOT SIMPLY "PUBLIC DOMAIN". An earlier revision of this file said it
was. Measurement disagreed: 774 of 861 routines are Apache-2.0 (Medsphere
lineage). Apache-2.0 combines cleanly into an AGPL work, but carries its own
attribution and licence-delivery duties — listed above and satisfied by
/opt/licenses/ inside the image.

The publication prerequisites this once waited on — the VA licence-posture
check and the combined-work disposition — are both closed (tracker PR-15,
PR-17). Building and using the image locally was never gated.

Not baked, and why (recorded so the decision is not silently revisited):
`alefragnani.Bookmarks` was evaluated as a companion extension and declares
GPL-3.0, which would add copyleft obligations to the IDE layer for a
convenience feature. It was refused on size grounds first; the license is a
second reason.
